# Example Caddyfile for reverse-proxying chasemapper with automatic HTTPS.
# See README.md "Deploying for Multiple Remote Users / HTTPS" for context.
#
# Caddy detects the WebSocket `Upgrade` header automatically, so no extra
# configuration is needed for the Socket.IO connection to work through it.
# Caddy also sets X-Forwarded-For automatically - set CHASEMAPPER_TRUST_PROXY=1
# on the chasemapper process to have it use that for real client IPs (see
# README.md "Behind a reverse proxy: set CHASEMAPPER_TRUST_PROXY").
#
# Replace chasemapper.example.com with your own DNS name, point it at this
# host, then run: caddy run --config Caddyfile

chasemapper.example.com {
    reverse_proxy localhost:5001
}
